<h3 style="color:#005EA5;border-bottom:2px solid #005EA5;padding-bottom:4px">What is a Confirmation Statement?</h3>
<p>Every UK company must file an annual Confirmation Statement (CS01) confirming that the information held by Companies House is accurate, including:</p>
<ul>
<li>Directors' names, addresses, and dates of birth</li>
<li>Registered office address</li>
<li>Share capital and shareholder details</li>
<li>SIC code (Standard Industrial Classification)</li>
<li>Persons with Significant Control (PSC) register</li>
</ul>

<h3 style="color:#005EA5;border-bottom:2px solid #005EA5;padding-bottom:4px">Consequences of Non-Filing</h3>
<ol>
<li><b>Strike-off:</b> The company will be struck off the register and dissolved after 2 months</li>
<li><b>Asset forfeiture:</b> All company assets (bank accounts, property, IP) become property of the Crown (bona vacantia)</li>
<li><b>Director penalties:</b> Directors may face personal liability and disqualification</li>
<li><b>Bank account freeze:</b> UK banks will freeze accounts of dissolved companies</li>
<li><b>Credit rating:</b> The company's credit rating will be adversely affected</li>
</ol>

