<h3 style="color:#005EA5;border-bottom:2px solid #005EA5;padding-bottom:4px">About GOV.UK One Login</h3>
<p>When you click "File Now", you will be redirected to <b>GOV.UK One Login</b> at <code>home.account.gov.uk</code> (the UK government's official identity platform). Depending on your company's configuration, you may see:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Company Authentication:</b> Enter your company authentication code (sent by post to your registered office)</li>
<li><b>GOV.UK One Login:</b> Enter your email and password</li>
<li><b>Identity verification:</b> If this is your first time using WebFiling, you may be asked to verify your identity by entering details from your passport or driving licence</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E8F1F8;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Security note:</b> GOV.UK Sign-in may ask for director personal information (passport number, date of birth, home address) to verify identity. This is a standard part of the UK government's identity assurance process for overseas directors. The URL will always be on a <code>.gov.uk</code> domain or an approved GOV.UK partner domain.
</p>

<p><b>Method 2 — File by post:</b></p>
